1
00:01:30,007 --> 00:01:40,007
Ah!

2
00:02:00,007 --> 00:02:07,907
But this is the sixth layer. If I go up, what about the curse?

3
00:02:08,187 --> 00:02:09,247
It's okay, Riko.

4
00:02:10,287 --> 00:02:14,867
I don't know exactly why this is, but the force field doesn't seem to exist here.

5
00:02:15,427 --> 00:02:17,247
So you won't get hit with the curse.

6
00:02:18,067 --> 00:02:21,887
Let's go on up. I want to learn more about these guys.

7
00:02:21,887 --> 00:02:35,127
I can't read consciousnesses here since there's no force field regs, so I'm counting on you to stay vigilant.

8
00:02:35,727 --> 00:02:36,207
Understood.

9
00:02:41,747 --> 00:02:44,767
Nanuchi, are these guys...hellows?

10
00:02:45,447 --> 00:02:51,267
Yeah, probably. But maybe they've retained their humanity somehow. They seem oddly intelligent.

11
00:02:51,887 --> 00:02:56,607
And the body of that one, Maji Kaja. What the heck is it made of?

12
00:02:57,047 --> 00:03:01,727
We need to know these types of things if we plan on going further. That's the sense I get.

13
00:03:02,167 --> 00:03:06,627
The Sovereign of Dawn spoke of this. It was something about curses and blessings, right?

14
00:03:06,867 --> 00:03:10,927
Who knows? But I hope this isn't the work of those white whistles.

15
00:03:10,927 --> 00:03:17,927
Imiti, it is here.

16
00:03:17,927 --> 00:03:21,927
Imiti, it is here.

17
00:03:21,927 --> 00:03:22,467
Pruska!

18
00:03:34,007 --> 00:03:34,527
What are you doing?!

19
00:03:34,527 --> 00:03:36,007
Right, hold on!

20
00:03:38,807 --> 00:03:41,367
Pruska...I think that... Pruska doesn't mind it.

21
00:03:42,267 --> 00:03:44,007
Huh?

22
00:03:44,007 --> 00:03:47,547
I think that Prushka doesn't mind it.

23
00:03:47,927 --> 00:03:48,307
Huh?

24
00:03:48,927 --> 00:03:50,107
Why not?

25
00:03:53,247 --> 00:03:56,887
Because the stone is not in its true form.

26
00:03:58,187 --> 00:03:59,227
Medipo.

27
00:03:59,567 --> 00:04:01,787
What was it in the common language?

28
00:04:02,307 --> 00:04:04,927
It gives sound to a life's will?

29
00:04:05,107 --> 00:04:06,247
Musical instrument?

30
00:04:06,567 --> 00:04:07,227
Yes.

31
00:04:07,527 --> 00:04:11,647
Upon becoming instruments, the stones get stronger and more precise.

32
00:04:11,647 --> 00:04:15,947
To possess one without undergoing the process is not good for value.

33
00:04:16,187 --> 00:04:16,587
Value?

34
00:04:21,927 --> 00:04:24,787
Come with me.

35
00:04:25,407 --> 00:04:27,747
Let Kaja show you to our Irohuru.

36
00:04:33,387 --> 00:04:35,907
Hey, Maji Kaja was it?

37
00:04:36,627 --> 00:04:38,727
Um, what in the world are you?

38
00:04:38,727 --> 00:04:43,267
A holo, just like that nice-smelling, fluffy one with you.

39
00:04:43,867 --> 00:04:44,347
Nah.

40
00:04:45,067 --> 00:04:49,647
Sorry for being the one to have to say this, but I'm not so sure you're even a living creature.

41
00:04:50,367 --> 00:04:52,407
Kaja's body is made of smells.

42
00:04:53,067 --> 00:04:55,047
Kaja cannot speak in that form.

43
00:04:55,667 --> 00:04:56,847
This body is a vessel.

44
00:04:57,907 --> 00:05:00,787
Kaja wanted a body, not a vessel.

45
00:05:00,787 --> 00:05:01,407
Kaja's body.

46
00:05:01,407 --> 00:05:18,847
Wow, what is this place?

47
00:05:19,367 --> 00:05:20,727
It's kind of like a market.

48
00:05:21,407 --> 00:05:23,047
Yes, right you are.

49
00:05:23,367 --> 00:05:25,147
A marketplace of value.

50
00:05:25,767 --> 00:05:29,127
Things and not things can be bartered based on value.

51
00:05:29,627 --> 00:05:30,107
Value?

52
00:05:30,107 --> 00:05:31,927
I'm still not sure what that means.

53
00:05:32,067 --> 00:05:34,427
Yeah, well, I bet it means something's true worth.

54
00:05:34,747 --> 00:05:36,467
Is the currency like back home?

55
00:05:36,747 --> 00:05:37,927
Doesn't seem like it.

56
00:05:38,627 --> 00:05:39,447
Hey, look here!

57
00:05:39,667 --> 00:05:41,487
These things used to belong to cave raiders!

58
00:05:41,967 --> 00:05:43,467
This one's antiquated.

59
00:05:44,007 --> 00:05:45,427
Must be from a long time ago.

60
00:05:46,487 --> 00:05:47,267
I wonder when.

61
00:05:48,927 --> 00:05:51,407
They all look to be in really good condition.

62
00:05:56,727 --> 00:05:59,347
No way, isn't this...

63
00:05:59,347 --> 00:06:01,747
Yeah, this is a section from Mother's letter!

64
00:06:01,967 --> 00:06:02,607
Napu!

65
00:06:02,967 --> 00:06:03,607
Napu!

66
00:06:03,607 --> 00:06:09,047
You must not touch that which has value without permission.

67
00:06:10,267 --> 00:06:12,507
Machi-Cacha, I want that piece of paper!

68
00:06:13,387 --> 00:06:17,707
You can obtain anything, as long as the value is in balance.

69
00:06:18,447 --> 00:06:20,607
It's possible for us to barter for that?

70
00:06:21,387 --> 00:06:23,847
Then which of my things can I trade for it?

71
00:06:23,847 --> 00:06:25,687
Let me check what I've got in here.

72
00:06:26,127 --> 00:06:27,067
You misunderstand.

73
00:06:27,667 --> 00:06:28,867
You, yourself.

74
00:06:29,667 --> 00:06:31,607
You would have a very good value.

75
00:06:32,147 --> 00:06:35,047
For instance, your eyes, skin, or fat.

76
00:06:35,747 --> 00:06:39,547
At the market, human children garner the most value.

77
00:06:39,547 --> 00:06:43,107
Kaja also wants one if it is whole and intact.

78
00:06:44,167 --> 00:06:49,527
Before you sell to someone else, I ask kindly that you speak to me first.

79
00:06:49,967 --> 00:06:50,867
No, wait!

80
00:06:51,287 --> 00:06:51,747
Not me!

81
00:06:52,167 --> 00:06:54,347
I'm going all the way to the bottom of the netherworld!

82
00:06:54,667 --> 00:06:55,487
A shame.

83
00:06:55,487 --> 00:06:57,247
Kaja concedes.

84
00:06:58,647 --> 00:07:02,167
Stealing value is the greatest of crimes.

85
00:07:02,727 --> 00:07:04,207
Well, I can't just give up.

86
00:07:04,647 --> 00:07:07,967
Can I buy it with my hair or nail clippings or something like that?

87
00:07:08,427 --> 00:07:11,427
So did you two see the symbol marked on the money?

88
00:07:11,747 --> 00:07:12,087
Yeah.

89
00:07:12,547 --> 00:07:13,867
It's that same symbol.

90
00:07:15,027 --> 00:07:18,567
Maybe Machi-Cacha doesn't actually know about that note then.

91
00:07:18,567 --> 00:07:25,887
Why don't we try to get more info by acting like we're interested in everything here?

92
00:07:26,147 --> 00:07:29,407
After all, the whole issue of who took Prushka seems to be forgotten.

93
00:07:30,267 --> 00:07:33,147
That's a good one, Reg getting used to enemy territory.

94
00:07:37,667 --> 00:07:38,187
Reg!

95
00:07:38,587 --> 00:07:39,067
Nanachi!

96
00:07:39,967 --> 00:07:41,407
Take a look over here!

97
00:07:41,567 --> 00:07:42,527
They're so cute!

98
00:07:43,307 --> 00:07:45,187
These hermit dwellers are for sale!

99
00:07:45,807 --> 00:07:46,947
And they're even alive!

100
00:07:46,947 --> 00:07:49,567
She's just being herself and enjoying this, huh?

101
00:07:50,087 --> 00:07:50,627
Me!

102
00:07:50,987 --> 00:07:51,327
Yeah!

103
00:07:52,067 --> 00:07:53,087
So adorable!

104
00:07:53,847 --> 00:07:57,127
Is this seller offering them as pets or are they for food?

105
00:07:57,367 --> 00:07:58,467
Neither, actually.

106
00:07:58,967 --> 00:07:59,787
But both.

107
00:08:00,527 --> 00:08:00,907
Hmm.

108
00:08:01,227 --> 00:08:07,007
This one, named Einbelitz, values small and adorable things crawling all over their body.

109
00:08:07,627 --> 00:08:10,307
The excess animals have been displayed for bartering.

110
00:08:11,567 --> 00:08:15,267
Kaja also trades as well, so as to make various vessels.

111
00:08:15,267 --> 00:08:20,887
Sabasa over there values passing tubes throughout their own body.

112
00:08:21,647 --> 00:08:26,167
Ah, and of course, Miss Keso values slicing apart the bodies of others.

113
00:08:26,947 --> 00:08:27,887
So, yeah.

114
00:08:28,687 --> 00:08:31,347
They sure do look the part now, don't they?

115
00:08:31,347 --> 00:08:37,627
You see, the bodies of all hollows more or less take on the shape of our respective desires.

116
00:08:38,727 --> 00:08:43,747
Every hollow here has challenged the netherworld, yet ended up with no place to go.

117
00:08:44,267 --> 00:08:46,427
Thus, we chose to remain here.

118
00:08:46,427 --> 00:08:53,567
When we offer our lives and turn into hollows, we become bound to this place and cannot leave.

119
00:08:54,427 --> 00:08:59,727
But in exchange, we receive protection in a form in line with our desires.

120
00:08:59,727 --> 00:09:03,227
You, nice smelling fluffy one.

121
00:09:03,847 --> 00:09:07,967
Unlike us, you are a hollow from the old ritual site, are you not?

122
00:09:08,747 --> 00:09:10,627
You possess true life.

123
00:09:11,527 --> 00:09:14,967
You must have been protected by a very powerful desire.

124
00:09:14,967 --> 00:09:22,307
It is of wonderful value.

125
00:09:22,307 --> 00:09:24,787
So, uh, you're just like me.

126
00:09:25,027 --> 00:09:29,427
You all dreamt of reaching the bottom of the abyss and settled on an adventure to explore it.

127
00:09:29,687 --> 00:09:32,907
I can't stay here, but it's very nice to meet you all.

128
00:09:32,907 --> 00:09:40,327
That's my friend, Mania, so play nice, okay?

129
00:09:41,867 --> 00:09:43,467
Hey, that tickles.

130
00:09:44,507 --> 00:09:46,047
Come on, stop it.

131
00:09:48,267 --> 00:09:48,827
Quit!

132
00:09:49,747 --> 00:09:51,687
Have a taste of your own medicine.

133
00:09:52,547 --> 00:09:53,347
Mania!

134
00:09:54,487 --> 00:09:55,087
No!

135
00:09:55,087 --> 00:09:56,747
Don't take me at me!

136
00:09:57,027 --> 00:09:57,807
Let me through!

137
00:09:58,187 --> 00:09:58,867
Stop it!

138
00:09:58,947 --> 00:10:00,547
Don't be so wrong with Mania!

139
00:10:00,767 --> 00:10:01,047
Yeah!

140
00:10:02,907 --> 00:10:04,307
Mania!

141
00:10:05,987 --> 00:10:06,387
Mania!

142
00:10:24,827 --> 00:10:25,467
It's all that you-

143
00:10:26,267 --> 00:10:26,647
Mania!

144
00:10:27,887 --> 00:10:29,327
Hey, move it!

145
00:10:29,427 --> 00:10:30,407
Out of my way!

146
00:10:30,767 --> 00:10:31,087
Yeah!

147
00:10:31,087 --> 00:10:33,827
Give me Mania.

148
00:10:36,827 --> 00:10:38,987
Well, what's with this?

149
00:10:39,447 --> 00:10:41,447
The bones are so soft.

150
00:10:43,287 --> 00:10:46,447
Whoa, hey now, stop moving around so much.

151
00:10:48,247 --> 00:10:48,847
Mania!

152
00:10:50,527 --> 00:10:53,007
Seems there wasn't anywhere for the air to go,

153
00:10:53,207 --> 00:10:54,907
so the butt guts plopped out.

154
00:10:55,907 --> 00:10:57,107
I'll push him back in.

155
00:10:57,887 --> 00:11:00,067
But it's gonna be swollen for a while.

156
00:11:00,067 --> 00:11:01,227
Ma, ma.

157
00:11:01,707 --> 00:11:03,827
Kefu, what is its value?

158
00:11:04,787 --> 00:11:07,807
No! Maybe it's not that kind of thing!

159
00:11:08,147 --> 00:11:10,667
Is it so high you cannot determine it?

160
00:11:11,087 --> 00:11:12,187
Yeah, that's right!

161
00:11:18,847 --> 00:11:20,367
Kefe de Kefu.

162
00:11:21,007 --> 00:11:22,147
Bevi mi hagu.

163
00:11:23,167 --> 00:11:25,967
Ah, the balancing begins.

164
00:11:30,067 --> 00:11:31,147
Ah!

165
00:11:35,687 --> 00:11:36,307
Ah!

166
00:11:36,707 --> 00:11:37,447
Ah!

167
00:11:37,647 --> 00:11:38,047
Hello?

168
00:11:42,107 --> 00:11:42,587
Ah!

169
00:11:51,847 --> 00:11:52,547
Ah!

170
00:11:52,547 --> 00:12:05,467
What is all that?

171
00:12:05,467 --> 00:12:10,807
As you have witnessed, that one caused damage to a value exceeding their own.

172
00:12:11,407 --> 00:12:12,727
It must be balanced.

173
00:12:13,747 --> 00:12:16,987
Things they have saved, things they have hidden.

174
00:12:17,727 --> 00:12:22,187
The balancing will not end until the values achieve equilibrium.

175
00:12:22,547 --> 00:12:38,007
Nanachi, are you okay?

176
00:12:38,227 --> 00:12:41,067
Don't worry. It's nothing, really.

177
00:12:41,987 --> 00:12:46,907
It is the room. The village understands the desires of its inhabitants.

178
00:12:46,907 --> 00:12:52,087
An undesired thing without buyers is transformed to a low value.

179
00:12:52,547 --> 00:12:55,627
Things that are changed into value are lost forever.

180
00:12:56,147 --> 00:13:00,047
Everyone here knows this, so we all abide by the protection.

181
00:13:00,267 --> 00:13:04,887
Yeah, but what if I were to tell you doing that doesn't make me feel any better?

182
00:13:05,447 --> 00:13:07,087
Is there a way you can make it stop?

183
00:13:07,827 --> 00:13:12,507
Iruburu. The protection of the village is so strong Kaja can do nothing.

184
00:13:12,507 --> 00:13:18,407
Or does it spell you so low there was actually no need for the balancing at all?

185
00:13:21,047 --> 00:13:23,467
It's not that. I just, uh...

186
00:13:23,467 --> 00:13:25,627
I just didn't want Mania to get hurt.

187
00:13:25,627 --> 00:13:37,107
The shortfall is compensated with the body.

188
00:13:37,527 --> 00:13:39,467
There are many buyers for bodies.

189
00:13:39,727 --> 00:13:42,687
For there are some who value knowing what's inside.

190
00:13:42,687 --> 00:13:49,067
Well, if stealing value is such a crime here, then how do you justify what happened with Prushka?

191
00:13:49,207 --> 00:13:52,307
That stone was brought from outside of Iruburu.

192
00:13:52,747 --> 00:13:56,847
Things that happen outside are not protected by the power of the village.

193
00:13:56,847 --> 00:14:00,127
So then, you're saying you aren't the ones who stole her?

194
00:14:00,307 --> 00:14:01,107
Hottie me.

195
00:14:02,487 --> 00:14:03,327
What the?

196
00:14:03,967 --> 00:14:05,887
Oh God, what's this?

197
00:14:06,587 --> 00:14:07,747
That is yours.

198
00:14:08,367 --> 00:14:11,487
It has finally reached the amount of your damaged value.

199
00:14:12,227 --> 00:14:12,667
What?

200
00:14:13,187 --> 00:14:15,727
But do I really have to accept this?

201
00:14:16,427 --> 00:14:21,087
Mayim, even if you were thrown away, it would not be discarded.

202
00:14:21,087 --> 00:14:23,907
The value is bound to you.

203
00:14:24,367 --> 00:14:25,807
Hanlisuku Hadi.

204
00:14:26,307 --> 00:14:27,727
How do I put it?

205
00:14:28,127 --> 00:14:31,447
You will not want for human food or a place to sleep.

206
00:14:32,207 --> 00:14:33,987
Kaja must take leave now.

207
00:14:34,587 --> 00:14:35,227
Farewell.

208
00:14:35,867 --> 00:14:36,927
Huh? Hold on!

209
00:14:37,507 --> 00:14:41,027
After what has happened, everyone now knows your value.

210
00:14:41,427 --> 00:14:43,827
Kaja believes no one will harm you.

211
00:14:43,827 --> 00:14:52,127
Hey, um, we're looking for some lodging for the night.

212
00:14:52,587 --> 00:14:54,347
Do you know of any place where we could stay?

213
00:14:55,547 --> 00:14:58,427
Uh, I'm not really sure how this is going to work.

214
00:14:58,927 --> 00:14:59,487
Hanlisuku?

215
00:14:59,847 --> 00:15:00,047
Huh?

216
00:15:00,807 --> 00:15:01,647
Mojimamodi.

217
00:15:02,247 --> 00:15:03,847
Uh, Hanlisuku.

218
00:15:04,087 --> 00:15:04,927
Mojimamodi.

219
00:15:07,327 --> 00:15:07,847
Hanlisuku.

220
00:15:08,527 --> 00:15:10,027
There's poop down there, Riko!

221
00:15:12,607 --> 00:15:13,267
What the?

222
00:15:13,267 --> 00:15:13,627
Huh?

223
00:15:14,207 --> 00:15:14,687
Kondos.

224
00:15:15,187 --> 00:15:15,707
Maybe.

225
00:15:19,707 --> 00:15:20,967
Oh, whoa!

226
00:15:21,187 --> 00:15:22,287
They understood that?

227
00:15:22,487 --> 00:15:24,527
Riko, how do you know to say that?

228
00:15:24,607 --> 00:15:28,727
Earlier, Maji Kaja said that word when talking about eating food in a place to sleep.

229
00:15:28,967 --> 00:15:29,927
Hanlisuku, right?

230
00:15:30,427 --> 00:15:30,947
Oh.

231
00:15:31,967 --> 00:15:33,167
You're pretty amazing.

232
00:15:33,787 --> 00:15:35,727
The language is difficult to decipher.

233
00:15:36,727 --> 00:15:40,107
At times like this, even if you don't know any of the native language,

234
00:15:40,107 --> 00:15:42,547
it's key to keep calm and make yourself understood.

235
00:15:42,547 --> 00:15:47,027
Also, when I lived up top, our orphanage held guided tours.

236
00:15:47,707 --> 00:15:50,547
But I admit I wasn't really all that good at it, though.

237
00:15:50,547 --> 00:15:57,487
We witnessed something awful, but you know, maybe more than anyone, Riko understands we

238
00:15:57,487 --> 00:16:00,287
can't afford to let ourselves get down at a time like this.

239
00:16:00,407 --> 00:16:00,747
Mm-hmm.

240
00:16:01,407 --> 00:16:03,947
Most likely, she just can't contain her excitement.

241
00:16:03,947 --> 00:16:11,847
Pardon, I'd like to rent a room for four of us, please.

242
00:16:12,227 --> 00:16:14,927
It would be me, Nanachi, Reg, and Mania.

243
00:16:14,927 --> 00:16:17,867
Do-do-do-do-do-do-do.

244
00:16:17,867 --> 00:16:20,487
I don't know how much it is.

245
00:16:20,487 --> 00:16:22,047
Nemo.

246
00:16:22,767 --> 00:16:24,007
Nemo.

247
00:16:24,187 --> 00:16:25,347
And some food as well.

248
00:16:25,587 --> 00:16:26,507
Nemo.

249
00:16:26,907 --> 00:16:29,027
I don't want to spend all of this.

250
00:16:29,167 --> 00:16:30,287
Makes me feel bad.

251
00:16:30,627 --> 00:16:32,167
But we kind of have to.

252
00:16:32,287 --> 00:16:35,207
After all, we need a safe place to treat Mania's injuries.

253
00:16:35,207 --> 00:16:41,827
So this is her room.

254
00:16:42,787 --> 00:16:44,427
This is the toilet.

255
00:16:45,007 --> 00:16:46,727
This is food.

256
00:16:58,087 --> 00:16:59,127
Oh, wow.

257
00:16:59,227 --> 00:16:59,927
That's crazy.

258
00:17:00,027 --> 00:17:00,987
It's not half bad.

259
00:17:01,687 --> 00:17:03,227
Yeah, you're right.

260
00:17:03,227 --> 00:17:11,847
Hey, given the color of this, and all the insects swarming in and around it, you sure

261
00:17:11,847 --> 00:17:12,347
it's okay?

262
00:17:12,487 --> 00:17:13,407
It tastes fine.

263
00:17:13,727 --> 00:17:17,847
Stuff that's horrible, like Nanachi's cooking, is honestly pretty rare.

264
00:17:18,407 --> 00:17:20,967
Besides, I bet we won't be able to eat this anywhere else.

265
00:17:21,307 --> 00:17:23,227
I don't want to miss my chance and regret it.

266
00:17:24,447 --> 00:17:26,827
This journey is a once-in-a-lifetime thing.

267
00:17:26,827 --> 00:17:29,027
Mm-hmm.

268
00:17:33,227 --> 00:17:36,627
I told you so.

269
00:17:36,987 --> 00:17:38,847
Need something to warm up your tummy?

270
00:17:39,567 --> 00:17:40,567
I'm okay.

271
00:17:41,067 --> 00:17:44,687
With this sort of thing, it's better to get diarrhea sooner than tired.

272
00:17:46,847 --> 00:17:47,407
Huh?

273
00:17:48,287 --> 00:17:49,147
Oh, oh.

274
00:17:49,267 --> 00:17:49,807
Bathroom!

275
00:17:50,747 --> 00:17:53,807
This is something I've seen countless times at the orphanage.

276
00:17:54,067 --> 00:17:56,607
She'll probably spend half the day glued to the toilet.

277
00:17:56,607 --> 00:17:58,447
What do you want to do today?

278
00:17:59,027 --> 00:18:02,387
I think I'll probably go look for things to help out Mania and Riko.

279
00:18:02,847 --> 00:18:04,147
You want to come with me?

280
00:18:08,227 --> 00:18:08,907
What's up?

281
00:18:09,127 --> 00:18:10,647
Where are all the hollows going?

282
00:18:17,267 --> 00:18:18,067
An earthquake.

283
00:18:18,487 --> 00:18:20,007
No, it was more like an impact.

284
00:18:22,267 --> 00:18:22,667
Majikaja!

285
00:18:22,667 --> 00:18:27,287
What's going on?

286
00:18:27,447 --> 00:18:28,307
What's that sound?

287
00:18:28,947 --> 00:18:29,467
Hadi.

288
00:18:30,507 --> 00:18:31,967
It must be Fapta.

289
00:18:32,507 --> 00:18:33,707
Kaja must see.

290
00:18:33,867 --> 00:18:34,347
Fapta?

291
00:18:35,047 --> 00:18:36,167
Very rare.

292
00:18:36,667 --> 00:18:38,267
Always very angry.

293
00:18:39,387 --> 00:18:41,747
Fapta is the embodiment of value.

294
00:18:42,287 --> 00:18:43,367
Can go anywhere.

295
00:18:43,707 --> 00:18:44,847
Will never perish.

296
00:18:45,247 --> 00:18:47,147
But usually stays away.

297
00:18:47,867 --> 00:18:49,247
Kaja wants to see.

298
00:18:49,687 --> 00:18:50,787
Did you hear that, Reg?

299
00:18:50,787 --> 00:18:51,427
Yeah.

300
00:18:51,807 --> 00:18:54,127
Fapta can go anywhere, but is rarely seen.

301
00:18:54,547 --> 00:18:57,487
It's probably the one who left us that nasty note, huh?

302
00:18:59,407 --> 00:19:00,547
Let's go, Nanichi.

303
00:19:01,007 --> 00:19:01,907
Wait, hold on.

304
00:19:02,307 --> 00:19:05,627
Leaving a sick Riko and an injured Mania behind makes me uneasy.

305
00:19:06,287 --> 00:19:07,667
Can I ask you to do some recon?

306
00:19:08,087 --> 00:19:09,127
Yeah, roger that.

307
00:19:09,567 --> 00:19:11,887
If anything comes up, I'll call on the comm device.

308
00:19:12,627 --> 00:19:14,007
Don't let your guard down.

309
00:19:14,207 --> 00:19:16,547
And turn back if you aren't sure what to do.

310
00:19:16,827 --> 00:19:17,487
Got it.

311
00:19:17,487 --> 00:19:20,747
What happened to the human child?

312
00:19:21,747 --> 00:19:24,147
She's dealing with a painful, upset stomach.

313
00:19:24,707 --> 00:19:26,647
Hadiva, that is not good.

314
00:19:26,947 --> 00:19:29,967
Kaja does not want the value of the human child to fall.

315
00:19:30,067 --> 00:19:34,027
Do you know where they sell clean water and fruit I can bring back to Riko for her stomach?

316
00:19:34,207 --> 00:19:35,327
Kaja will guide you.

317
00:19:35,767 --> 00:19:39,487
Hadiva, though Kaja wants to see Fapta, but Kaja...

318
00:19:40,267 --> 00:19:41,047
Which one will it be?

319
00:19:41,047 --> 00:20:07,387
Well, about this Fapta, what exactly are we talking about?

320
00:20:07,387 --> 00:20:09,987
Hadiva, yes.

321
00:20:10,567 --> 00:20:13,847
The meaning of Fapta in the common language is...

322
00:20:13,847 --> 00:20:15,567
How do you say it?

323
00:20:16,107 --> 00:20:18,307
A high status female.

324
00:20:18,927 --> 00:20:19,467
Oh, yeah?

325
00:20:20,087 --> 00:20:21,587
She a princess or something?

326
00:20:22,147 --> 00:20:23,347
Yes, correct.

327
00:20:23,807 --> 00:20:24,547
A princess.

328
00:20:26,227 --> 00:20:29,047
Princess of the hollows.

329
00:20:29,047 --> 00:20:43,807
What?

330
00:20:44,807 --> 00:20:46,507
Are they asking us something?

331
00:20:47,047 --> 00:20:47,947
We are Ganja.

332
00:20:48,647 --> 00:20:51,487
A group of explorers in search of the hidden Golden City.

333
00:20:53,427 --> 00:20:54,387
It's listening.

334
00:20:54,387 --> 00:20:58,007
They're sussing out our intentions based on reactions.

335
00:20:58,927 --> 00:21:00,427
And likely our speech patterns.

336
00:21:00,987 --> 00:21:01,747
This is great.

337
00:21:01,927 --> 00:21:02,567
I love it.

338
00:21:02,747 --> 00:21:04,107
I feel their intelligence.

339
00:21:05,787 --> 00:21:06,187
Ganji.

340
00:21:06,867 --> 00:21:09,427
You think they want us to follow them?

341
00:21:10,027 --> 00:21:11,407
Everyone, stay on your guard.

342
00:21:11,407 --> 00:21:24,347
Oh, my gosh.

343
00:21:26,487 --> 00:21:27,827
The Golden City.

344
00:21:28,447 --> 00:21:29,627
We're really here.

345
00:21:29,627 --> 00:21:31,627
Oh, my gosh.

346
00:21:31,627 --> 00:21:35,787
Oh, my gosh.

347
00:21:35,787 --> 00:21:38,867
The Golden City.

348
00:21:38,867 --> 00:21:39,547
We're really here.

349
00:21:41,407 --> 00:21:50,047
We had finally arrived.

350
00:21:51,107 --> 00:21:53,367
But after our long, arduous adventure,

351
00:21:54,507 --> 00:21:56,167
we had still been unable

352
00:21:56,167 --> 00:21:59,167
to find a way to survive.

353
00:23:29,950 --> 00:23:59,930
Thank you.

